The three techniques to be discussed are zero-shot, few-shot, and fine-tuned inference. Note that these techniques have a long history related to transfer learning research in NLP. To be honest, the idea of "adapting" a pre-trained model to fit into the downstream tasks is not new. Older NLP architectures such as Proximal Policy Optimization and Monte Carlo Tree Search also have similar techniques in which a "pre-trained" policy executed before tailored to the environment. We will now discuss the three techniques, starting from the easiest-to-use to the most labor-intensive approach.

