    num_return_sequences: Optional[int] = None,
    decoder_start_token_id: Optional[int] = None,
    use_cache: Optional[bool] = None,
    **model_kwargs,
)
```
The input to the function is a `input_ids` tensor, which is a tensor of shape `(batch_size, sequence_length)` that contains the IDs of the input sequence. It can be omitted, in which case the model will generate text from scratch.

The output of the function is a tensor of shape `(batch_size, num_return_sequences, sequence_length)` that contains the IDs of the generated text.

Here is a brief description of some of the most commonly used options:

* `max_length`: The maximum length of the generated text.
* `min_length`: The minimum length of the generated text.
* `do_sample`: Whether to use sampling or greedy decoding.
* `num_beams`: The number of beams to use when generating text.
* `temperature`: The temperature parameter used for sampling.
* `top_k`: The number of top candidates to keep for top-k sampling.
* `top_p`: The cumulative probability of the top P candidates for nucleus sampling.
* `repetition_penalty`: The penalty applied to repeated n-grams.

