Post by: Nanoof , Greenhorn
No, if you add ResourceUtils.CLOSE_CONTEXT_WHEN_EMPTY, automatic closing on close.
This is indeed what occurs, when the stream calls close() on the InputStream, it will send an EOS as well.

                    with spring "echo"     without echo
write 0             EOS|Resource          EOS|Resource
write 1             Resource|1|EOS           1|EOS
write 0             EOS|Response         EOS|Response with no chunk writing
write 0             EOS|Response         EOS|Response with chunk writing

Well I found out that currently the HttpExchange might cause a "Suspect header last modified value" error (change of last modified header with HTTP/1.1) when using ChuckResource that is created dynamically with echo turned on. To fix this you just have to add the header explicitly and make sure it is never overwritten.

To get rid of the echo all together, refer to HTTP 1.1. the protocol states that the sender (your server in this case) has to include a closing of connection signal (content length and or EOS), else the client will never know if another chunk will follow.

