A non-scientific method for calculating this would be to simply measure the wattage with no load on the interfaces, and then again with the interfaces fully loaded. The difference will be the power used to run the interfaces, divided by the number of prompts per second will give you the power per prompt.

This approach doesn't account for any marginal load or reductions in power based on traffic patterns, etc. But it should give you a good *rough* figure which should be sufficient for sourcing bids on power usage and such.

