**[UPDATE 2023/07/24]**

Having exchanged a few messages with OpenAI support, I got a proper solution for this:

Instead of messages:

```
[
    {"role": "user", "content": "Say something"},
    {"role": "assistant", "content": "Hi!"}
]
```

you can use funcs:

```
[
    Functions(
        name="chat_completion",
        description="Makes a ChatCompletion API call. Returns the generated response as the assessed case.",
        parameters=FunctionsParameters(
            returnType="object",
            parameters=[Parameter(name="max_tokens", type="integer", minimum=1, maximum=4096)]
        )
    ): functions.chat_completion(max_tokens=30),
    FunctionsArguments(
        pass_assistant_content=True,
        pass_assistant_source="gpt-3.5-turbo",
        pass_sys_prompt="System prompt suggesting use of the AI model to simulate a court case, and suggest drafts for use by the lawyer.",
        pass_user_assistant_messages=[
            {
                "role": "system",
                "content": "You are a lawyer explaining a case to another lawyer. Use the AI model to simulate the court, evaluate the case, and suggest a draft for use by the lawyer. Keep the AI-generated response neutral, without taking any sides. Start by saying 'Without taking sides: ...'. Focus on presenting the case to the opposite lawyer with probative facts, legal points, and arguments. Consider including the relevant laws to support the case. Avoid completely copying and pasting case documents. Instead, summarize the pertinent information, and adapt it for effective communication in a virtual court. Remember, the goal is not to win the case by aggressiveness, but to present a strong, persuasive, and legally defensible position."
            }
        ],
        assistant_function_call="chat_completion",
        assistant_function_call_arguments={
            "max_tokens": 30
        }
    )
]
```

OpenAI support also made it clear, that even though you can pass `functions` in a call, what’s supposed to be used is `FunctionsCall`:

```
FunctionsCall(
    name="chat_completion",
    arguments={
        "max_tokens": 30
    }
)
```

